  "term": "registered nurse",
  "definition": "A registered nurse is a nurse who completed an accredited nursing program, passed a state licensing exam, and is licensed by a state authority to practice. Educational preparation may come through hospital diploma, associate degree, baccalaureate, or combined programs.",
